  "readingHtml": "<h1>Alex's Busy Day</h1><div class=\"subtitle\">Present Simple vs. Present Continuous</div><p><span class=\"para-label\">A.</span>Alex is a 15-year-old student and a football player. He <b>usually</b> wakes up at 7 o'clock. He eats a <b>healthy</b> breakfast and goes to school. After school, he <b>trains</b> with his team. They <b>play</b> a <b>match</b> every Saturday.</p><p><span class=\"para-label\">B.</span>Today is different. Right now, Alex is at the <b>stadium</b>. It is the final of a big <b>tournament</b>. Look! The <b>coach</b> is talking to the players. Alex is running with the ball. He is going to <b>score</b> a goal!</p><p><span class=\"para-label\">C.</span>After the match, Alex will <b>rest</b>. He needs to sleep because he is very tired. Tomorrow, he will put his <b>equipment</b> in the bag and go back to school.</p>",
